From: lab <lab@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:56:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] LAB: protocol detection in the log entry, the UI and the
 access rules

Local lab branch; not for upstream as-is.

- Log: the detector's observation rides the TUNNEL_CLOSED entry as a nested
  pd block (own schema version, closed vocabularies, absent when nothing was
  observed). Host names go through the keyed destination pseudonymizer.
  Advisory signals: nonstandard_port, host_mismatch, server_unresolved.
- Policy: PolicyRule.AppRestriction restricts the protocol families allowed
  on the raw tunnels an Allow rule permits. Monitor records what enforce
  would do. Enforce holds the client's first bytes (bounded, prebuffer
  included) until the client direction is decided, so no client byte of a
  disallowed protocol reaches the server. The unknown action is explicit and
  also applies when the detector is unavailable. A block is logged as
  APP_BLOCKED.
- UI: new frontend (frontend/): Traffic gets an Application / Protocol
  column, a protocol-mix bar and an evidence panel in the row detail; the
  Access Rule editor gets the protocol restriction; the rules list shows it.
  The legacy page gets the same column. frontend/dist is rebuilt with the
  pinned Node 24.19.0.
- Tests: decision table, validation and signals (Go); pd decoder (vitest).

